  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Quiescent weather expected through the end of\nthe week.\n\nCurrent surface analysis depicts that the cold front has largely\npushed through the region this morning. In its wake, drier air\nis building in from the west and we are starting to see a few\nwind gusts around 20 mph, though very sparse at this time. As\nwe mix out later this morning into the afternoon, winds will\nincrease to 10 to 15 mph with gusts of 20 to 25 mph. An\noccasional gust near 30 mph near higher terrain. Despite the \npassage of the front, downsloping winds likely pushing temps \nwell into the 70s to near 80 for most. Lowered Tds given the \ndownsloping setup NBM was not catching at all.\n\nSeasonable (albeit slightly cooler) temps and dry conditions \nwill then persist under high pressure Fri through Fri\nnight. Lowered Tds in aft given recent NBM issues and favorable\nsetup for lower Tds.\n\nHigh pressure retreats off to the NE Sat with cloudcover from\nthe remnants of Isaias moving in and thickening through the day.\nAny precip likely holds off until Sat night or Sun morning. \n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...Remnants of Tropical Storm Isaias arrive late this \nweekend.\n\nTropical Storm Isaias continues to be the main weather feature to \nmonitor over the forecast period with remnants expected to impact \nthe forecast area later this weekend. The National Hurricane Center \nhas TS Isaias tracking a bit slower and further east than previous \nforecasts, with remnant circulation over central Kentucky early \nSun afternoon. Dry conditions are expected for the forecast \narea through Sat, with precip associated with remnants of \nIsaias reaching the forecast area on Sun. The most likely \nimpact to the forecast area continues to be rain although severe\nweather cannot be ruled out on Sunday. Most likely rainfall is\nan inch or two, but still highly uncertain. This many days out,\nthe track, timing, and impacts of Tropical Storm Isaias remain \nuncertain so be sure to monitor hurricanes.gov for the latest \nforecast.",
